From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0755: present_stats export: 0750's display counters as one exported struct (rex_present_stats), for the in-game statistics screen

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (T7 overlay, 2026-11-27)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: 0750 only logs what the display really showed (every present_stats_log_s seconds, from a private class of the D3D12
  presenter). The title's in-game statistics screen needs the same numbers a few times a second. This mirrors the counters into
  one exported struct of relaxed atomics, extern "C" rex_present_stats (size, version 1, then cumulative presents, retired, shown,
  dropped, sync_refreshes, sync_qpc, qpf, held[4] = shown frames that stayed 1, 2, 3, 4+ refreshes, over_cadence = frames held
  longer than the cadence allows, cadence_milli, valid). The reader subtracts two reads. Fed from the same places as 0750's own
  counters (so only while present_stats_log_s > 0): six relaxed atomic adds per Present, no lock, no allocation. No behaviour
  change. The reader's copy of the layout is src/host/overlay/present_stats_abi.h in mcla-x86.
Bucket: REDO

0755-present-stats-export.patch (mcla-x86 T7).

---
diff --git a/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp b/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp
--- a/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
